NAME
       signal, raise, sigemptyset, sigaddset - signal helpers

SYNOPSIS
       #include <signal.h>

       void (*signal(int sig, void (*fn)(int)))(int);
       int raise(int sig);

       int sigemptyset(sigset_t *set);
       int sigfillset(sigset_t *set);
       int sigaddset(sigset_t *set, int sig);
       int sigdelset(sigset_t *set, int sig);
       int sigismember(const sigset_t *set, int sig);
       int sigaltstack(const stack_t *ss, stack_t *old);

DESCRIPTION
       signal is the simple way to install a handler; sigaction(2) is
       the one to use when the mask or the flags matter. raise sends a
       signal to the caller.

       The set functions build the masks passed to sigprocmask and
       stored in a sigaction.

       A handler runs on a frame the kernel builds on the user stack
       and returns through the trampoline in libc, so ordinary C code
       works inside one. Keep it short and touch only volatile
       sig_atomic_t state.

RETURN VALUE
       signal returns the previous handler or SIG_ERR; the rest return
       0 or -1 with errno set.

SEE ALSO
       kill(2), sigtest(1)
